Requirements: 18   with obligations: 17   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Make the model requests of a single review run share their opening text.
    Content that several of a run's requests carry is written the same way in each of
    them and placed at the front, ahead of the content that is unique to the request.
    Where a provider must be told where the reusable opening ends, the client tells it,
    and no individual request does.
    -> share-opening-text-across-run-requests  [functional/explicit]
       The model requests of a single review run share their opening text, with shared
       content written the same way in each request and placed at the front ahead of
       request-unique content.
    -> client-marks-reusable-opening-end  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-05)
       Where a provider must be told where a request's reusable opening ends, the client
       marks that boundary and request-building code does not.

[constraint-01] Content carried by more than one of a run's requests is byte-identical
    in each request that carries it.
    -> shared-content-byte-identical-across-requests  [invariant/explicit]
       Content carried by more than one of a run's requests is byte-identical in each
       request that carries it.

[constraint-02] Each request orders its content by how widely that content is shared
    across the run's requests: content carried by more of them precedes content carried
    by fewer, and content carried by that request alone comes last.
    -> shared-content-ordered-by-breadth  [functional/explicit]
       Each request orders its content by how widely that content is shared across the
       run's requests: content carried by more of them precedes content carried by
       fewer, and content carried by that request alone comes last.

[constraint-03] Two requests of one run that share content share it as a leading run of
    bytes, not as a fragment somewhere inside them.
    -> shared-content-leading-run-of-bytes  [invariant/explicit]
       Two requests of one run that share content share it as a leading run of bytes,
       not as a fragment somewhere inside them.

[constraint-04] Reordering a request changes only the order of what it carries; it
    carries the same content afterwards as before.
    -> request-reordering-preserves-carried-content  [functional/explicit]
       Reordering a request leaves the request carrying the same content, with only the
       order of that content changed.

[constraint-05] Where a provider must be told where a request's reusable opening ends,
    the client marks it and no request-building code does.
    -> client-marks-reusable-opening-end  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01)
       Where a provider must be told where a request's reusable opening ends, the client
       marks that boundary and request-building code does not.

[constraint-06] The client does not mark a reusable opening shorter than the shortest
    one the provider in use can reuse.
    -> reusable-opening-not-shorter-than-provider-minimum  [boundary/explicit]
       The client marks a reusable opening that is at least as long as the shortest
       reusable opening the provider in use can reuse.

[exclusion-01] What any stage is asked, and what content any stage receives. This task
    changes the order and the wording of content already carried, and adds none.
    -> no-change-to-asked-or-received-content  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter what any stage is asked or what content any stage
       receives.

[exclusion-02] Which stages exist, how a stage divides its work across calls, and how
    large those divisions are.
    -> no-change-to-stage-structure-or-call-partitioning  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter which stages exist, how a stage divides its work across
       calls, or how large those divisions are.

[exclusion-03] Model calls issued by the measurement harness, which is not part of a
    review run.
    -> no-change-to-measurement-harness-model-calls  [compatibility/explicit]
       The change does not affect model calls issued by the measurement harness.

[exclusion-04] Whether a provider in fact reuses any part of a request it was offered,
    which is the provider's own behavior and not this tool's.
    -> no-claim-about-provider-reuse-behavior  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not assert or depend on whether a provider actually reuses any
       part of an offered request.

[exclusion-05] Reporting tokens, cost or reused-token share, which a run already
